{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/srsz10","slideIndex":0,"text":"Source: NEW COPY DOC.docx, Chapter I, Conceptual Model of the Project, and user-provided conceptual-model image. Input details are grouped for slide readability. Knowledge includes document forensics and the 15-category taxonomy, prompt engineering, Google GenAI integration, web development and RESTful APIs, SQLite/SQLAlchemy, JWT authentication, three-tier RBAC, mobile UI/UX, Python and FastAPI. Software includes Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Uvicorn, SQLAlchemy, SQLite, React, React Router, React Native, Vite, PWA, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Visual Studio Code and Cloudflare. Hardware includes a computer or laptop, internet, and an implementation server with at least 4 GB RAM. Process: Requirements, Design, Development, Testing, Deployment, Review. Output full title: Revelator: An AI-Assisted Web and Mobile App Document Forgery Analysis System using Gemini Vision. Evaluation: System Usability Scale (SUS) and ISO/IEC 25010 Software Quality Evaluation."}